<title>UK: State of Hessen sets 100 mln mark step-up bond. [CORRECTED 14:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>State of Hessen sets 100 mln mark step-up bond. [CORRECTED 14:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects to show that the deal carries an investor put option after 10 years and not a borrower call option)</p>
<p>The following putable bond was announced by lead manager Baden Wuerttembergerische Bank AG.</p>
<p> BORROWER   STATE OF HESSEN</p>
<p> AMT    100 MLN DEM   COUPON    *6.0	 MATURITY    30.OCT.26</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  99.50     PAY DATE    30.OCT.96</p>
<p> LISTING     LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10	 GOV LAW    GERMAN</p>
<p> NOTES     *RISING TO 7.625 PERCENT IF AN INVESTOR PUT OPTION 		AFTER 10 YEARS IS NOT EXCERCISED.</p>
<p>		FEES WERE UNDISCLOSED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
